 "verdicts": {
  "Opsera announced on October 29, 2026 its relaunch as an AI-native software factory with Forge at its center, described as a governed, spec-driven software factory for modernizing legacy estates and building new applications.": 1,
  "Opsera claims it can shorten time to market from two weeks to two days, cut token use by up to 75%, save up to $10 million in operating costs, and reduce security reviews from eight weeks to hours.": 1,
  "Opsera's Forge acts as an enterprise AI harness that turns legacy logic, architecture and business intent into reusable living specs and execution-ready work orders, with a human in the loop and evals, security and compliance checks at every stage.": 1,
  "Opsera's Forge integrates with Anthropic, OpenAI, GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Antigravity, DeepSeek and Devin, and Opsera connects more than 150 tools; it runs in cloud, on-premises or hybrid environments.": 1,
  "Opsera's ForgeScore assesses legacy codebases across eight dimensions: security, maintainability, system gravity, production resilience, cognitive load, logic narrative, semantic clarity and future proofing.": 1,
  "Opsera's Unified Insights uses tokenomics and token mapping to connect AI spend to results across tools, teams and workflows; the portfolio also includes Forge for Salesforce and Forge for Databricks.": 1
 }
